@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] marvin-launch-boundary
The extension MUST transmit a source page only after an explicit toolbar click,
only for the four exact HTTPS provider hosts, and only to the configured server.
It MUST NOT collect page contents, credentials, history or telemetry.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] marvin-package-boundary
Archives MUST contain only maintained extension assets and generated build
metadata. The package version MUST come from package.json; archives MUST have
stable entry order, timestamps, modes and compression for identical inputs.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] marvin-checked-javascript
Maintained JavaScript, including build scripts and tests, MUST pass strict
TypeScript checking through explicit JSDoc interfaces. External values MUST be
validated before use; dependency tools MUST remain outside distributed archives.
